<title>TURKEY: Japan and Turkish Airlines sign joint flight deal.</title>
<headline>Japan and Turkish Airlines sign joint flight deal.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkish Airlines announced it had signed an accord with Japan Airlines (JAL) to launch joint services to carry JAL passengers in THY's round-trip Osaka-Istanbul flights from November.</p>
<p>According to the agreement, six business and 70 economy class seats will be reserved for JAL passengers in the THY flights scheduled twice a week.</p>
<p>THY also said in a statement that the number of round-trip flights would be raised to three a week.</p>
</text>
